graph TD
    accTitle: A table as table, row and cell nodes
    accDescr: A table node holds row nodes and each row holds cell nodes; each cell keeps its column name, so a single cell such as a recommendation number can be found and returned with its row.
    TableNode["Table Node<br>(audit:table::1)"]
    Row1["Table Row Node<br>(table::1:row::1)"]
    Row2["Table Row Node<br>(table::1:row::2)"]
    
    Cell1["Cell Node: Rec No<br>(10/2025/01)"]
    Cell2["Cell Node: Status<br>(Awaiting Response)"]
    Cell3["Cell Node: Implementer<br>(Operations Unit)"]

    TableNode -->|part_of| Row1
    TableNode -->|part_of| Row2
    
    Row1 -->|part_of| Cell1
    Row1 -->|part_of| Cell2
    Row1 -->|part_of| Cell3
